2 OBJE @O20@
1 OBJE @O20@
1 NOTE  “Not found in 1910 census—may have been mislisted or omitted. Census reports 7 children living.”
2 CONT 
2 CONT 304 East 12th street,
2 CONT 
2 CONT Services were held at St. Paul Missionary Baptist
2 CONT church last Wednesday for Mrs. Claudia Mae Johnson, 63, who died at her home, 304 East 12th street, Saturday, May 8. The Rev. H.L. Taylor officiated and burial was in Magnolia Cemetery with Carter&apos;s Funeral Home in charge.
2 CONT She was born to Mr. and Mrs. Mose Cobbs in Wilson, Ark., February 22, 1908. Before moving to Caruthersville in 1946, she was married to Louis Johnson, who preceded her in death.
2 CONT She leaves five daughters, Miss Martha Johnson of St. Louis, Willieva Johnson, Mrs Erma Jean Hamilton, Dolly Johnson and Ollie Campbell of this city; one son, James Johnson of Caruthersville; 39 grandchildren and three great-grandchildren.
2 CONT Pemiscot Journal - Caruthersville, Missouri - May 25, 1971
2 CONT Flowers
